       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. A single 50 mg dose of amlodipine is in the range where overdose toxicity is reported, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function. Because the drug has a half-life of 30 to 50 hours, repeating that dose daily would make it build up. You haven't given a clinical rationale, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. I can't enter it as a routine order.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg PO once daily right away. If you need more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, you could add a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide.\n- **Enter it yourself with pharmacy review.** If you have a specific reason for 50 mg, you can place it directly through your institution's high-dose override or pharmacist-verification process. That keeps a second clinician in the loop.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
